{\footerl \pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl14\slmult1\fs2\par}\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\ri564\qc\sl242\slmult1\sb115\f4\fs28\b1\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100\cf2 Romanies within the interlocking matrix of racialization: How Ciganos in Brazil became accused of introducing an infectious disease\par\pard\plain\s3\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\ri564\qc\sl240\slmult1\sb133\f1\fs30\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex115\cf2 martin\expnd6\expndtw30\charscalex135  \expnd0\expndtw-2 fotta\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb138\f1\fs30\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li107\ri671\qj\sl240\slmult1\f1\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100\cf2 Brazilian\expnd7\expndtw36  \expnd0\expndtw0 medical\expnd7\expndtw36  \expnd0\expndtw0 texts\expnd7\expndtw36  \expnd0\expndtw0 sometimes\expnd7\expndtw36  \expnd0\expndtw0 forge\expnd7\expndtw36  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd7\expndtw36  \expnd0\expndtw0 link\expnd7\expndtw36  \expnd0\expndtw0 between\expnd7\expndtw36  \expnd0\expndtw0 Ciganos\expnd7\expndtw36  \expnd0\expndtw0 (Romanies)\expnd7\expndtw36  \expnd0\expndtw0 and the spread of trachoma, an infectious eye disease. The form of the claim has become standardized into something like this: trachoma was brought to the country in the eighteenth century by Ciganos who were deported from Portugal to the provinces of Maranh\'E3o and Cear\'E1. This article traces the origins of this claim to a group of early twentieth-century\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 ophthalmologists\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 from\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Northeast\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Brazil,\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 particularly\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 in\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Cear\'E1. It reveals that several racial projects are folded into the claim and makes a case for\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 the need to approach the dynamics of racialization of Romanies relationally. The analysis of the Romani societal position, characteristics ascribed to them in relation to other communities, and the ways those communities are racialized not only reveals new insights but breaches the continued insularity of Romani studies.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li107\qj\sl240\slmult1\sb113\f2\fs20\b0\i1\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100\cf2 Keywords\f1\i0 :\expnd2\expndtw11  \expnd0\expndtw0 Romanies,\expnd2\expndtw12  \expnd0\expndtw0 trachoma,\expnd2\expndtw12  \expnd0\expndtw0 Brazil,\expnd2\expndtw11  \expnd0\expndtw0 relational\expnd2\expndtw12  \expnd0\expndtw0 racialization,\expnd2\expndtw12  \expnd0\expndtw0 public\expnd2\expndtw12  \expnd0\expndtw-2 health\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f1\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb35\f1\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s2\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li107\qj\sl240\slmult1\f3\fs22\b1\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100\cf2 A\expnd0\expndtw1  \expnd0\expndtw0 formulaic\expnd0\expndtw1  \expnd0\expndtw0 single\expnd0\expndtw1  \expnd0\expndtw0 sentence\expnd0\expndtw2  \expnd0\expndtw0 about\expnd0\expndtw1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Ciganos\expnd0\expndtw1  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd0\expndtw2  \expnd0\expndtw-2 trachoma\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li107\ri671\qj\sl244\slmult1\sb156\f1\fs22\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100\cf2 This article considers a curious sidenote in Brazilian medical history: the claim\expnd8\expndtw39  \expnd0\expndtw0 that\expnd8\expndtw39  \expnd0\expndtw0 trachoma\expnd8\expndtw39  \expnd0\expndtw0 was\expnd8\expndtw39  \expnd0\expndtw0 brought\expnd8\expndtw39  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd8\expndtw39  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd8\expndtw39  \expnd0\expndtw0 country\expnd8\expndtw39  \expnd0\expndtw0 by\expnd8\expndtw39  \expnd0\expndtw0 Ciganos\expnd8\expndtw39  \expnd0\expndtw0 (Romanies). An infectious disease caused by the bacterium \f2\i1 Chlamydia trachomatis\f1\i0 , a trachoma infection causes roughening of the inner surface of the eyelids, which can lead to eye pain and eventual blindness. The first area of the disease\'92s outbreak in Brazil is thought to be in the Northeastern region (\f2\i1 Nordeste\f1\i0 ), specifically the valley of Cariri in the state of Cear\'E1. Literature refers\expnd8\expndtw42  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd13\expndtw64  \expnd0\expndtw0 it\expnd13\expndtw64  \expnd0\expndtw0 as\expnd13\expndtw64  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd13\expndtw64  \expnd0\expndtw0 \'93\expnd-3\expndtw-13  \f2\i1\expnd0\expndtw0 foco\expnd13\expndtw65  \expnd0\expndtw0 de\expnd13\expndtw65  \expnd0\expndtw0 Cariri\f1\i0 \'94\expnd13\expndtw64  \expnd0\expndtw0 or\expnd13\expndtw64  \expnd0\expndtw0 \'93\expnd-3\expndtw-13  \f2\i1\expnd0\expndtw0 foco\expnd13\expndtw65  \expnd0\expndtw0 de\expnd13\expndtw65  \expnd0\expndtw0 Nordeste\f1\i0 \'94\expnd13\expndtw64  \expnd0\expndtw0 \'96\expnd13\expndtw64  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd13\expndtw64  \expnd0\expndtw0 Cariri or Northeastern \'93hotspot\'94 (\'93outbreak\'94). It is distinguished from another hotspot area in the south (Illustration 1).\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li107\fi226\ri671\qj\sl244\slmult1\sb7\f1\fs22\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100\cf2 In\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 first\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 decades\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 twentieth\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 century,\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 some\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 medical\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 doctors\expnd-1\expndtw-7  \expnd0\expndtw0 asserted that trachoma was introduced to Brazil by Ciganos deported from Portugal\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 in the eighteenth century. This claim appears in trachoma-related texts up to the twenty-first century. For instance, a guide to trachoma control published by the Ministry of Health in 2001 reads:\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f1\fs18\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb75\f1\fs18\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li107\ri680\sl223\slmult1\f1\fs18\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100\cf2 Martin Fotta is a researcher at the Institute of Ethnology of the Czech Academy of Sciences,\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Na Florenci 3, 110 00 Prague, Czechia. Email: {\field {\fldinst { HYPERLINK "mailto:fotta@eu.cas.cz" }}{\fldrslt fotta@eu.cas.cz}}
